      "raw": "<p>(If this has been discused already just point me to the proper place and ignore me)</p><p>My copy of Vengance arrived just ahead of a snow storm so today I&#39;ve had great opportunity to finaly see the V5 in action. I&#39;ve also seen some discusion here about the idea of future additions to the V5 and ideas of using existing villains as V5 alternates. It occured to me that the Eenead might be kind of a natural fit with them from a mechanics perspective. The numbers and card counts seem to support it. If you choose a single character card from the Eennead remove the others, the shrine and the 4 cards that cause you to place new character cards into play you have the same number of cards as a V5 deck and a villain character card with roughly equal HP to the other V5 characters. Other than that it seems that it would just work normaly.</p><p>I haven&#39;t yet tested this idea though. Thoughts?</p>",
